      "content": "Using leftover antibiotic pills, especially another antibiotic after finishing a prescription, is not advisable and could be ineffective or harmful. It's not a substitute for a personalized medical evaluation. Also, if your immune system is affected by the infection, increasing your dose might not help and could cause harm by either not treating the infection or by experiencing side effects. Chills and graduating the spread of red streaking indicate that your body's response to the infection isn't just restricted to minor symptoms. I suggest you rest, keep the wound clean, and get in touch with healthcare professionals for assistance. It's best to avoid taking unnecessary medication, as it might complicate your condition. Rest is your body's way of fighting the infection, so try to get some rest and seek professional advice. Your safety and health are crucial.",
